Package: libva-v4l2
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, v4l-utils
Provides: va-driver
Description: VA-API backend for Qualcomm Iris stateful V4L2 devices
 Hardware video decoding through the Qualcomm Iris stateful V4L2 M2M
 interface, for SM8550 and SM7475 (Xiaomi Poco F5 / Redmi Note 12 Turbo,
 marble). Requires a kernel whose Iris driver exposes the decoder (see the
 iris decode-order patch in linux-redmi-marble) and a matching firmware.
 .
 Decoded frames reach the client through one of three publish policies
 chosen per surface: Direct (the completed CAPTURE slot itself is handed
 over), Import (a buffer the client exported before its first decode is
 queued into CAPTURE, which is the zero-copy path Chrome takes) and Copy
 (GPU blit inside a stable buffer, used for VP9 and on stock kernels
 without the decode-order controls). Nothing here selects the policy by
 hand; the driver reads the client's export behaviour.
 .
 Includes the MSM driver alias, the GStreamer VA environment
 configuration, and the iris-vaapi-browser launcher with a
 "Google Chrome (Iris VA-API)" desktop entry. Decode only: the backend
 exposes no VAEntrypointEncSlice, so no H.264/HEVC encoding is offered.
